  "notes": "{読|よ}みふける is an intransitive ichidan verb. Compound of {読|よ}み (reading) + ふける (to be absorbed in). The auxiliary ふける attaches to other verb stems as well (e.g., {考|かんが}えにふける, {物思|ものおも}いにふける).\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{読|よ}みふけっている describes the ongoing state of being absorbed in reading.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {本|ほん}に{読|よ}みふける (to be engrossed in a book)\n- {小説|しょうせつ}に{読|よ}みふける (to be absorbed in a novel)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {小説|しょうせつ}に{読|よ}みふける (to be lost in a novel)\n- {本|ほん}に{読|よ}みふける (to be absorbed in a book)\n- {一日中|いちにちじゅう}{読|よ}みふける (to read all day long)",
